WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.920
Welcome to today's deep dive. I mean imagine you build this pristine like five-star luxury car

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:12.680
But when you go to sell it the dealership insists on paying you the price of a rusted used bicycle

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:17.120
That is exactly what is happening to Puerto Rico's health care system right now

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:22.720
Yeah, it really is a massive contradiction when you dig into the CMS data consoles and enrollment research

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:28.960
You see this glaring anomaly. I mean Puerto Rico has the highest medicare advantage penetration in the entire US

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:34.200
Right over 96% exactly 96.2% and they are getting top tier clinical quality yet

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:39.120
They receive the absolute lowest federal health care funding in the nation and for you listening

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.480
This isn't just some you know boring policy quirk

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:48.200
This is a masterclass in how massive gaps in federal funding actually force a local market to innovate just to survive

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:54.000
So true and to understand why practically everyone chooses medicare advantage or MA over traditional medicare

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:56.280
We really have to look at what they aren't getting

00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:00.560
Let's compare say Elena in Puerto Rico to Rosa in Florida, okay?

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:06.040
So both are paying the exact same medicare payroll taxes their whole lives, right?

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:11.200
But Rosa in Florida has access to this whole federal safety net. She gets

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:14.400
supplemental security income medicare savings programs

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:20.200
Part D extra help for prescriptions and long-term care Medicaid and Elena in Puerto Rico

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:23.400
She gets none of that right none of it. She is completely excluded

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:30.320
So that creates a federal support gap of roughly three thousand four hundred dollars a month Wow three fee four hundred dollars every single month

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:35.440
That is huge it is and it makes standard traditional medicare basically useless for Elena

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:40.680
If she wanted full coverage like standard medicare plus a medigap policy and a drug plan

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:47.000
She'd be paying around four hundred fifty dollars a month out of pocket which on a fixed income in Puerto Rico is literally impossible

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:51.440
So she chooses medicare advantage because it steps in and offers a zero dollar premium

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:57.840
Yeah, and they bundle in vital supplemental benefits to stuff traditional medicare ignores like dental vision and transportation

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:00.040
It's kind of like traditional medicare is a smartphone

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:03.960
But for someone in Puerto Rico the battery in the screen are sold separately

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:10.160
Yeah, so MA plans essentially manufacture their own batteries and give away a fully working phone for free

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:12.520
Just to patch those holes in the safety net

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:15.440
That's a perfect way to put it but here is where it gets wild

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:21.680
You would assume given they rely entirely on MA with such limited funds that the care would be bare bones

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:26.360
But it's actually the exact opposite wait really how good are we talking well?

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:32.680
99.1% of Puerto Rican MA patients are enrolled in plans rated 4.5 stars or higher by CMS

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:37.960
The three largest five-star MA contracts in the entire US are in Puerto Rico

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:41.440
Okay, hold on. I have to jump in here if they are delivering five-star care

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:45.400
Shouldn't the federal government be rewarding that I mean Puerto Rico's benchmark is only

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:50.200
$778 a month right well the US average is over $1300

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:52.720
Yeah, $1313 to be exact

